# X2-PROVISIONAL and SI2-PROVISIONAL — the runs behind @pixagram/paph-x 1.1.1's screen fixes
#
# docs/PAPH-X.md §6 and docs/SPEC-SI-paph-si.md cite these.  rust/target/release/{sibench,xbench}
# (cargo build --release); the PAPH-SI corpus from 'sibench corpus' (120 bases x 21 variants +
# 8,000 distractors) and 'sibench corpus --bases 0 --distractors 100000 --from 8000 --out corpus-big.bin';
# the PAPH-X corpus is built in process by xbench (344 works, 2,379 pairs); test/x-bench.mjs reads it
# from 'xbench --dump rust/target/xcorpus' for its last two tables.
# Machine: Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz, 2 cores, shared container; timings on one core.
# Counts, classes and recalls are deterministic; timings are this run's and move by several per cent.
# 1.1.0's runs (X1, SI1) are docs/calibration/SI1-PROVISIONAL.log.

